# INV-06 — invented. Five overs a side; retirements of every kind.
# Edge cases: a batter retiring hurt at the start of an over and resuming
# once a wicket has fallen (not a wicket, his figures carried on); a batter
# retiring out at the non-striker's end (a wicket with no ball: falls at the
# last ball bowled, 1.6); a batter timed out (a wicket, no ball faced, no
# bowler's wicket); a retired-hurt batter who never comes back ("retired
# hurt", not out and not a wicket); a first innings defended.
